### What can the server do? { video: bool (needs ffmpeg), maxBytes }
GET http://localhost:5005/api/media/capabilities

### Upload a picture, GIF, WebP, BMP, JPEG or (with ffmpeg) video. 201 -> { id, name, kind, width, height, frames, durationMs }
### 400 unsupported/corrupt, 413 too big (Media:MaxBytes, default 25 MB), 503 video without ffmpeg, 507 library full (Media:MaxLibraryBytes)
POST http://localhost:5005/api/media
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ledboundary

--ledboundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="name"

My animation
--ledboundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="anim.gif"
Content-Type: image/gif

< ./anim.gif
--ledboundary--

### curl equivalent
# curl -F "file=@anim.gif" -F "name=My animation" http://localhost:5005/api/media

### List the library
GET http://localhost:5005/api/media

### Thumbnail (PNG, at most 128 px wide, first frame)
GET http://localhost:5005/api/media/{{id}}/thumb

### Delete (204)
DELETE http://localhost:5005/api/media/{{id}}

### Play it: pick the app, then choose items (comma separated ids; empty = everything) and how to show them
POST http://localhost:5005/api/apps/media

###
POST http://localhost:5005/api/apps/media/settings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": "{{id}}", "mode": "Fit", "seconds": 10, "loops": 0, "speed": 100, "background": "#000000", "shuffle": false, "brightness": 100 }

### The picker behind the Items setting (lists the library; q narrows by name)
GET http://localhost:5005/api/apps/media/settings/items/options?q=
